{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerFactorial","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerFactorial","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qGeneric_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qGeneric_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L148-L155","doc":"**Genericity from positivity (sorry-free).**  For real `q > 1`, the\nparameter genericity `QGeneric q n` holds — the form Wenzl's\ncriterion consumes — recovered here from the quantum-factorial\nroute (`qFactorial_ne_zero_of_one_lt` + `qFactorial_ne_zero_iff`),\nagreeing with the direct order-arithmetic proof in\n`WenzlSchurElement`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_ne_zero_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_ne_zero_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L138-L146","doc":"**The real substrate is generic at every rank (sorry-free).**  Any\nreal `q > 1` — in particular the substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` — has\n`[n]_q! ≠ 0` for every `n` (indeed `> 0` by `qFactorial_pos`): no\nquantum integer vanishes, so the parameter-side hypothesis of\nWenzl's criterion is discharged.  Bridges to\n`WenzlSchurElement.wenzlGeneric_of_one_lt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_pos","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L128-L136","doc":"**The quantum factorial is positive for `q > 0` (sorry-free).**  A\nproduct of positive quantum integers.  In particular it is nonzero,\nstrengthening the genericity fact in the archimedean substrate\nregime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_pos","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L120-L126","doc":"**Quantum integers are positive for `q > 0` (sorry-free).**  `[n]_q`\nis a sum of positive powers, hence strictly positive for `n ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_ne_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_ne_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L92-L114","doc":"**The genericity equivalence (sorry-free).**  For `q ≠ 1` over a\nfield, the quantum factorial is nonzero iff `q` is generic at rank\n`n`:\n\n  `[n]_q! ≠ 0  ⟺  ∀ k ∈ [2, n], q^k ≠ 1`.\n\nThis is the arithmetic (parameter) half of Wenzl's semisimplicity\ncriterion for `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QGeneric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QGeneric","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L88-L90","doc":"**Parameter genericity** (field form of `WenzlSchurElement.WenzlGeneric`):\n`q` is not a `k`-th root of unity for any `2 ≤ k ≤ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_succ","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L81-L86","doc":"**Quantum-factorial recursion** `[n+1]_q! = [n]_q! · [n+1]_q`\n(sorry-free) — the induction step for Schur-element / Gram\ncomputations over `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_one","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L78-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial_zero","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L75-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qFactorial","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L71-L73","doc":"The **quantum factorial** `[n]_q! = ∏_{k=1}^{n} [k]_q` — the Poincaré\npolynomial of the Iwahori–Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_succ","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L67-L69","doc":"**Quantum-integer recursion** `[n+1]_q = [n]_q + q^n` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L56-L65","doc":"**Vanishing of a quantum integer.**  For `q ≠ 1`,\n`[k]_q = 0 ⟺ q^k = 1` — i.e. `q` is a `k`-th root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_eq_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_eq_div","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L51-L54","doc":"Closed form `[n]_q = (q^n - 1)/(q - 1)` for `q ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_one","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_zero","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L39-L45","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical geometric bracket.**\n\n`qInt` is kept rather than aliased: `qInt_eq_div` below does\n`rw [qInt, geom_sum_eq hq]`, which needs the `Finset.sum` to be the literal\nbody. The two are definitionally the same object, so the consolidation here is\nthis equation — checked, not asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qInt","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QIntegerFactorial.lean#L36-L37","doc":"The **quantum integer** `[n]_q = 1 + q + ⋯ + q^{n-1} = ∑_{i<n} q^i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}